{"title":"NOBL Wheels Launches AR Series of All-Road Wheels With Its Lightest Rims to Date","link":"https://bikerumor.com/nobl-wheels-launches-ar-series-of-all-road-wheels-with-its-lightest-rims-to-date/","date":1793994153000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-54-1536x1024.jpeg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"(All photos / NOBL Wheels)\" /></p>\n<p>Yesterday, <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/?s=NOBL\">NOBL Wheels</a> expanded its product lineup with the introduction of the AR Series of all-road wheels. The new AR40 and AR50 wheelsets are built with the brand’s lightest road rims to date, starting at just 350 grams (AR40). These new AR Series rims combine NOBL’s aerodynamic teardrop profile with 25mm internal widths and fully hooked beads to support increasingly wide road tires. The complete wheelsets are available in the more affordable Core version with NOBL hubs, or Custom builds with several hub and spoke options. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12.jpeg\"><img width=\"1067\" height=\"711\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12.jpeg\" alt=\"the NOBL AR40 wheels on a road bike.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12.jpeg 1067w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-12-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>NOBL AR Series Rim Design</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>First introduced on the <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/nobl-far-series-wide-light-gravel-racing-wheels/\">FAR gravel race wheels</a>, the AR Series rims utilize NOBL’s aerodynamic teardrop rim profile. This design has the widest point of the rim not at the bead wall, but slightly below it. This is intended to help with aerodynamics when used with wider tires by smoothing around the bulbous leading and trailing edges. NOBL says “<em>It meets the rule of 105 with a 30c tire, which measures about 32mm on the AR’s 25mm internal width</em>.” </p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1575\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions-1536x1575.jpeg\" alt=\"cutaway profile and dimensions of the NOBL AR40 rim\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions-1536x1575.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions-293x300.jpeg 293w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions-117x120.jpeg 117w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions-768x788.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions-1498x1536.jpeg 1498w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions-878x900.jpeg 878w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Profile-Dimensions.jpeg 1950w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1535\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions-1536x1535.jpeg\" alt=\"cutaway profile and dimensions of the NOBL AR50 rim\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions-1536x1536.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions-900x900.jpeg 900w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Profile-Dimensions.jpeg 2001w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>With a 25mm internal width and fully hooked beads, the AR-Series rims are designed for broad tire compatibility. NOBL states they are ready for tires from 28-45c and pressures up to 80 psi, with the confidence and security of a hooked bead. Riders can also ride with confidence knowing that NOBL offers a lifetime warranty on its carbon rims and lifetime service on its wheelsets, including truing, tensioning, and cleaning.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41.jpeg\"><img width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41.jpeg\" alt=\"a man riding a road bike with the NOBL AR40 wheels\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41.jpeg 1600w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Stef-Curtis-Ti-Landyachtz-Low-Res-41-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Weight</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>NOBL says that its new AR Series rims are its lightest road rims to date. They used T1000 carbon and their most advanced layup process to create what they say is among “<em>the lightest and strongest 25mm internal road rims with a hooked bead</em>.” The claimed weight of the 40mm deep AR40 rim is 350 grams, while the 50mm deep AR50 rim is a touch heavier at 380 grams. Despite the low weights, NOBL says the AR40 has passed impact testing up to 110J, while the AR50 has a 115J impact rating.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Of course, these lightweight rims result in lightweight wheelsets. The complete Core wheelset with NOBL hubs weighs a claimed 1307g (AR40) /1367g (AR50). The lightest Custom wheelset — DT180 hubs, Berd Polylight spokes, XDR driver — is claimed to weigh 1124g (AR40) /1184g (AR50). </p>\n\n\n\n<h3>AR Series Specs</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-AR-Specs.jpeg\"><img width=\"937\" height=\"572\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-AR-Specs.jpeg\" alt=\"screenshot of a chart with the NOBL AR Series Specs\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-AR-Specs.jpeg 937w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-AR-Specs-297x181.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-AR-Specs-120x73.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-AR-Specs-768x469.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>NOBL Core AR40 / AR50 Wheelset</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Rims: NOBL AR40 / AR50</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hubs: NOBL Core Road Hub, 36t Ratchet</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Spokes: Alpina Extralite / Sapim CX-Ray</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Nipples: Black</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brake Interface: Centerlock </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Driver: XDR / MS Road / HG</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Graphics: 4 Colour Options</li>\n\n\n\n<li>$1,999.00 CAD | $1,599.00 USD</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wheelset Weight: 1307/1367g (Alpina Extralite Spokes, XDR Driver)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-Core-AR40-Wheelset-White-BG-1500.jpeg\"><img width=\"1500\" height=\"1500\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-Core-AR40-Wheelset-White-BG-1500.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the NOBL AR40 Core wheelset\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-Core-AR40-Wheelset-White-BG-1500.jpeg 1500w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-Core-AR40-Wheelset-White-BG-1500-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-Core-AR40-Wheelset-White-BG-1500-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-Core-AR40-Wheelset-White-BG-1500-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NOBL-Core-AR40-Wheelset-White-BG-1500-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-1536x1536.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the NOBL AR50 Core wheelset\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-1536x1536.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-2048x2048.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR50-Core-Wheelset-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n<figcaption>NOBL offers 4 decal options: gloss black, gloss white, chrome silver, and chrome gold.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>NOBL Custom AR40 / AR50 Wheelset </h2>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Rims: NOBL AR40 / AR50</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hub Brands: DT Swiss / Chris King / Hope / Project 321 / Onyx / Industry Nine / SON</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Spokes: Alpina Extralite / Sapim CX-Ray / Berd Polylight</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Nipples: Black</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brake Interface: Centerlock</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Driver: XDR / MS Road / HG</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Graphics: 4 Colour Options</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Starting at $2,279.00 CAD | $1,699.00 USD</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Lightest Wheelset Weight: 1124/1184g (DT180 Hubs, Berd Polylight Spokes, XDR Driver)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75.jpeg\"><img width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75.jpeg\" alt=\"a man riding with the NOBL AR40 wheels on his road bike.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75.jpeg 1600w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/AR40-Road-Cole-Glover-Factor-Ostro-Low-Res-75-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Availability</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>NOBL’s new AR Series all-road wheelsets are available now. Head to the NOBL website to learn more about the Core and Custom builds, or order a set today.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://shop.noblwheels.com/ar-series\">noblwheels.com</a></em></p>","author":"Jeremy Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/nobl-wheels-launches-ar-series-of-all-road-wheels-with-its-lightest-rims-to-date/#respond","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"0991d9c3d4de12afaf8cb30b87f4cae9031ad886c8beda323b980ac5d1bad615","category":"Cycling"}